case-organizer (4.9.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * The home-screen app no longer gets stranded when the site is briefly
    unreachable. A standalone container has no address bar to refresh from, and
    WebKit kept handing back the edge's cached 502 across relaunches, so the app
    looked permanently dead and even re-adding the shortcut did not clear it. A
    service worker now replaces any failed page load with a recovery page that
    polls /ping and continues on its own once the origin answers. It caches
    nothing belonging to the app, so it cannot serve anything stale, and it
    leaves every API call, upload and form post untouched.
  * The date picker works on a phone. The calendar button drove a 1px input
    parked off-screen through showPicker(), which iOS does not implement, and
    the click() fallback does nothing on a hidden control, so the button was
    simply dead. The real picker is now laid invisibly over the button and
    receives the tap itself.
  * Administrator settings are usable on a phone. The users, legal notice and
    certificate tables were 6-column layouts behind a sideways scroller, which
    left the Actions column off the right edge where it could not be reached.
    Each row is now a card with labelled fields, and every control is a 44px
    target.
  * A stray dropdown arrow no longer floats in the right margin. The arrow is an
    absolutely positioned pseudo-element, and without a positioned trigger it
    anchored to the page rather than to its own field.
  * Dates read dd/mm/yyyy throughout. Stored timestamps were shown in the
    database's own YYYY-MM-DD form, and the calendar's long dates followed the
    browser's locale, which puts the month first on a US-configured machine.
  * Removed a stale 190 KB copy of main.js that was being packaged and shipped.

 -- Izumi <swarajswarupaggarwal@gmail.com>  Sat, 08 Aug 2026 16:45:00 +0530

case-organizer (4.9.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Large uploads no longer fail behind Cloudflare. Files at or over 80 MB are
    sliced into 16 MB parts, sent to /api/upload/chunk and reassembled server
    side, keeping every request under the 100 MB body limit the tunnel enforces.
    The assembled file re-enters the normal upload handler, so it faces the same
    extension whitelist and magic-byte checks as a direct upload.
  * Reopening a completed task works again. Editing status from Done back to
    Pending left the completion timestamp in place, and the overdue test
    requires it to be empty, so the task could never become overdue again.
  * Completing a late task keeps its history. Previously every day it had run
    over silently became an ordinary entry the moment it was ticked off; those
    days stay marked overdue and the entry records how many days late it was.
  * Deleting an entry, or marking one done, can be undone. A banner appears
    across the foot of the calendar for nine seconds with an Undo button; it
    holds while hovered. Restoring brings back the entry with its assignees,
    participants and reminders intact.
  * Adjourning now requires the date it was adjourned to, and creates the
    follow-up entry on that date carrying the same case, purpose and assignees,
    linked from the original.
  * Home-screen icons are packaged. 4.9 shipped the apple-touch-icon link
    without the file behind it, because the icons directory and manifest were
    never listed in the install manifest; iOS fell back to drawing a letter.
  * Upgrades no longer re-run first-install work. postinst never checked whether
    a previous version was configured, so the Postfix/debconf setup and a
    recursive chown ran on every deploy.
  * Mobile fixes: sheets scroll instead of passing the gesture to the page
    behind them (calendar.css was overriding the scroll container); sheets can
    be pulled down to dismiss from anywhere in the sheet, with a single grip
    centred above the header; the sticky modal header no longer lets content
    show above the title; and date fields stop overflowing Create Case.

