case-organizer (4.9) stable; urgency=medium

  * Mobile front end. The app is now usable on a phone, built entirely in the
    front end: a media query below 640px plus a script block that exits
    immediately on anything wider. No template, route or backend change, so the
    desktop layout and workflow are untouched.
    - Every interactive control is at least 44px tall, and inputs render at
      16px so iOS stops zooming on focus.
    - Multi-column forms stack. .form-card is a grid whose implicit column
      sizes to max-content, which pushed the Manage Case fields 18px past the
      screen edge and took 30 elements off-screen with them.
    - Modals become full-width sheets with their own scroll container, a
      sticky header, and a sticky action bar, so Save and Cancel stay reachable
      on a long form. Previously the action row sat below the fold, under the
      phone's address bar, and the mobile navigation bar painted over it.
    - A bottom navigation bar and a drawer listing every page, built by cloning
      the account menu the server already renders, so it cannot drift and stays
      correct per role. The drawer names the signed-in account, and logout
      leaves the top bar entirely rather than sitting under the thumb.
    - The card that opens a form now holds it directly beneath itself, with the
      remaining cards pushed below; only one form is open at a time.
    - Calendar: the day agenda is a sheet you push into (tap to select, tap
      again to open) instead of a side column below the fold. Month grid shows
      per-day dots; the month navigation no longer runs off both edges.
    - Invoice: the A4 line-item table becomes one labelled card per item, and
      every contenteditable value renders as a real, visible field.
    - Long-press on a search result opens the case action menu as a bottom
      sheet, since there is no right-click on a phone.
  * Manage Records: each legal notice and certificate can now be downloaded as
    well as deleted, via /api/certificates/<id>/download and
    /api/legal-notices/<id>/download (admin only, path-checked against the
    storage root).

