case-organizer (4.8) stable; urgency=medium

  * Calendar / event manager — timed scheduling & recurrence. Every event
    defaults to all-day but can be given a start (and optional end) time.
    Tasks, deadlines and the new "Meeting / Conference" event type can
    repeat hourly / daily / weekly / monthly / yearly (with an interval and
    an optional end date); occurrences are expanded at view time, so one
    stored rule drives the whole series without bloating the database.
  * Continuing tasks & deadlines. A task or deadline can be marked
    "continuing": once overdue it rolls forward and shows on every day until
    it is marked complete. Overdue is now time-aware (a timed item becomes
    overdue after its time on the day; an all-day item the next day).
    "Mark complete" lets you choose the completion date — including
    back-dating; a back-dated completion removes the item from later days
    while the days it occupied stay visible, annotated "completed on …", so
    the history of when things were finally done is never lost.
  * Reminders. Any event can carry reminders that are emailed AND delivered
    to each assignee's in-app inbox: at the event's time, at a set time on
    the day (handy for all-day matters), or repeating every 30 min / hour /
    day starting a chosen lead time before the event. An in-process
    scheduler fires them every minute; reminders on a recurring event
    re-arm to the next occurrence.
  * Schema migration v9 -> v10: case_events gains all-day/time, recurrence
    and completion columns and the new event_reminders table; a reserved,
    login-disabled system account is added as the sender of automated inbox
    messages (hidden from the user list and the setup guard). Existing
    events are unchanged (all-day, non-recurring, non-continuing).
  * Manage Case overhaul. The case picker now matches the calendar — a
    party-name search on top with a year/month/case browser below (no more
    lookup tabs). Once a case is picked you choose a File Category and then a
    Subcategory (the main proceeding / cause of action); both sit ABOVE the
    Primary vs Misc tabs, which stay faded until they are set. Primary files
    the main pleadings directly under the subcategory. Misc files one of a
    FIXED set of interlocutory applications — the interim remedies the CPC /
    CrPC / Commercial Courts Act provide (stay, injunction, receiver,
    attachment, amendment, condonation, discharge, exemption from appearance,
    …) — within that same subcategory, as Case/<Subcategory>/<Misc
    application>/; a misc application is not a fresh subcategory. When the
    case's Our Party is the respondent (read from Note.json — fixed at case
    creation, no toggle) the subcategory list is swapped for the responsive
    pleadings (Written Statement, Counter Affidavit, Reply, Cross-Objections
    …). The proceedings area is always on screen, faded until a case is
    selected; Main Type sits just before the date; and Generate Invoice /
    View Note are grouped bottom-right.
  * Subcategory taxonomy is grouped by forum / statute instead of one flat
    list — Commercial, for example, keeps Commercial Suits, Banking & Finance
    (DRT / SARFAESI), each IP right, Insolvency, Company Law, Competition,
    Securities, Arbitration, Direct Tax (ITAT) and Indirect Tax (CESTAT / GST)
    as separate groups. Tax prosecutions stay under Criminal (Economic
    Offences), not Commercial.
  * Standard sub-folders. Every subcategory / proceeding directory can now
    receive uploads into a fixed set of sub-folders — Primary Documents,
    Case Law, Research, Annexures, Drafts, Notes, Court Copies, Pleadings,
    Judgments & Orders — created on demand.
  * Daily digest PDF. The morning digest email now attaches a one-page PDF
    with a proper table of the day's listings, filings / deadlines due,
    overdue items and tomorrow's schedule — including event times and each
    item's assignees. The plain-text body is kept as a fallback.
  * Tests: added coverage for timed/recurring events, continuing-overdue
    rollover and back-dated completion, reminder firing (email + inbox),
    nested misc-proceeding uploads with the standard sub-folders, and the
    daily-digest PDF rendering.

