case-organizer (4.6.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Admin Settings: administrators can now permanently delete a user
    account, not just deactivate it. A "Delete" button sits beside
    "Deactivate/Activate" in each user row — the two share the row width
    equally — and asks for confirmation before removing the account. The
    delete is guarded so you cannot remove your own account or the last
    active administrator; deleting a user also revokes their sessions and
    (via the schema's foreign keys) removes their messages, password-reset
    tokens and event assignments, while invoices, certificates, notices and
    calendar events they authored are kept with the author cleared. Backed
    by the admin-only Settings "delete_user" action and a new
    services.users.delete_user() helper.
  * Tests: added delete_user service tests (removal, cascade of sessions,
    missing-user no-op) and Settings route guard tests (admin can delete
    another user; self-deletion is refused).

