    and division headers shown in the dropdown. Case Law, Invoices, and
    Legal Notices keep no subcategory. Advanced Search uses the same list.
  * Manage Case upload: File Subcategory folder names containing "/" (e.g.
    "Section 482 CrPC / Section 528 BNSS") are flattened to a single safe
    folder, and the upload target is now validated with _safe_path().
  * The View/Edit Note.json modal was updated to the same Category-only
    classification and Original + Current Status court model, with
    backward-compatible loading of existing notes (legacy current-court
    values map to a sensible status).
  * Certificate generator: stamps a centred "CERTIFICATE OF INTERNSHIP"
    title automatically; the proforma band is now a single line (Date on the
    left, Certificate No on the right). The intern name and internship dates
    come from the uploaded document and are no longer collected. Margins are
    measured from the selected letterhead (matching Legal Notices),
    reclaiming first-page working room.
  * UI: searchable dropdown inputs and options now inherit the surrounding
    font size instead of a fixed 14px so they match neighbouring fields;
    empty group dividers no longer appear while typing an uncatalogued court.
  * UI: the case-law "Name" search (Petitioner / Respondent / Either Party)
    now spans the full card width with each option stacked on its own row.
  * Tests: added tests/test_cases.py (classification + court model and File
    Subcategory folder safety); suite now 156 tests.
